  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sathish vs Food Safety Officer on 19 November, 2024 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh Bench: N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD)No.1 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 19.11.2024 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD) No.10665 of 2023 and Crl.M.P. (Md) No.8484 of 2023 1. Sathish 2. Anandh ... Petit Vs. Food Safety Officer, Karur, Code No.429, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, District Collector Office Campus, Karur District. ... Res Prayer : Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 482 of Criminal Procedure Code, to call for the records pertain to the ord passed in CMP.No.2912 of 2023 in C.C.No.637 of 2022 on file of Learned Judicial Magistrate Court No.I, Karur, dated 18.4.2023 and aside the same as illegal. For Petitioners : Mr.R.Karunanidhi For Respondent : Mr.B.Thanga Aravindh Government Advocate (Crl. Si 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.10 Sathish vs Food Safety Officer on 19 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/132767841/ 1 Order",
    "facts": "3.The petitioners were facing a private complaint initiated by the respondent for offences under Sections 51, 52(i), 58, 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The summons was issued to the petitioners and the petitioners were asked to be present before the Court below. Hence, they filed the petition on 10.04.2023 by expressing their intention to contest the case on merits. 5.The Court below through the impugned proceedings dated 18.04.2023, dismissed the application and posted the matter for pronouncing judgment. Aggrieved by the same, the present petition was filed before this Court.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
